{"type":"standard","title":"Mike Rogers (Michigan politician)","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Mike Rogers (Michigan politician)</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q970515","titles":{"canonical":"Mike_Rogers_(Michigan_politician)","normalized":"Mike Rogers (Michigan politician)","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Mike Rogers (Michigan politician)</span></span>"},"pageid":412632,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Mike_Rogers_in_November_2019_%283x4_cropped%29.jpg/330px-Mike_Rogers_in_November_2019_%283x4_cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":441},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6d/Mike_Rogers_in_November_2019_%283x4_cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":822,"height":1099},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1378760041","tid":"c5fff580-c126-11f1-b85a-b60ce4a1cc51","timestamp":"2026-10-06T01:39:30Z","description":"American politician (born 1963)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mike_Rogers_(Michigan_politician)","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mike_Rogers_(Michigan_politician)?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mike_Rogers_(Michigan_politician)?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Mike_Rogers_(Michigan_politician)"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mike_Rogers_(Michigan_politician)","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Mike_Rogers_(Michigan_politician)","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mike_Rogers_(Michigan_politician)?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Mike_Rogers_(Michigan_politician)"}},"extract":"Michael J. Rogers is an American law enforcement officer and politician who served from 2001 to 2015 as the U.S. representative for Michigan's 8th congressional district. A member of the Republican Party, he chaired the United States House Permanent Select Committee on Intelligence from 2011 to 2015.","extract_html":"<p><b>Michael J. Rogers</b> is an American law enforcement officer and politician who served from 2001 to 2015 as the U.S. representative for Michigan's 8th congressional district. A member of the Republican Party, he chaired the United States House Permanent Select Committee on Intelligence from 2011 to 2015.</p>"}